module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.deleted_ci_job_survives_at_the_branch_head_that_predates_its_deletion

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data deleted_ci_job_survives_at_the_branch_head_that_predates_its_deletion: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "deleted_ci_job_survives_at_the_branch_head_that_predates_its_deletion" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a deleted CI job keeps running, on every branch whose head predates the deletion, and the PR it blocks never touched the workflow** (the workflow that executes is the one AT THE PULL REQUEST'S HEAD, not the one on the default branch, so deleting a job stops it for main and for nothing else. Every branch cut before that commit keeps a full copy of the old roster and keeps paying for it, once per push, until someone integrates the deletion. ",

    "INVALID STATE: a head whose workflow roster is a superset of the default branch's, carrying a job whose lane no longer exists anywhere else, with an aggregating job that waits on it. The branch is then structurally unable to go green: the deleted lane cannot conclude, the aggregate cannot resolve, and no amount of fixing the diff changes either. ",

    "HARM IS PAID TWICE AND BOTH HALVES ARE INVISIBLE FROM THE DIFF. In runner time: the specimen's job held an arm64 runner for three hours per run, on a lane the operator had already deleted, and it re-armed on every push. In attention: the PR shows pending checks with no failure to read, so the reader's first hypothesis is the change in front of them -- which is the one thing that cannot be responsible, because the diff does not touch the workflow at all. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the tell is cheap and mechanical: compare the job roster in the workflow AT THE HEAD against the roster on the default branch, or ask `git merge-base --is-ancestor <deletion commit> <head>` directly. A job present at the head and absent on main is this class, full stop; the diff's contents are irrelevant to the diagnosis, which is exactly what makes it hard to see from the diff. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT ITS TWO NEAREST NEIGHBOURS, and the boundaries matter because each one sends the repair somewhere else. It is NOT [[instruction_and_subject_resolved_from_different_revisions]]: there, the instruction and the tree come from DIFFERENT revisions and the split is the defect. Here they agree -- the workflow and the tree are both at the head, perfectly consistent with each other -- and the defect is that the agreed-upon instruction is one the world has since deleted. It is NOT [[stale_base_branch_reads_as_pending_work]] either: that class is about CONTENT that has already landed, and its repair is to close the branch; this branch's content is unlanded and wanted, and its repair is to integrate one commit. ",

    "THE SIBLING SHAPE IN THE SAME MECHANISM, worth stating because the fix for one does not fix the other: the workflow's `pull_request` trigger is also filtered on the BASE branch, so a PR based on a session branch rather than on the default branch gets no runs at all -- not delayed, structurally absent. Both are the same root fact read from two ends: WHICH workflow runs, and WHETHER it runs, are decided by the pull request's own refs and not by the default branch's current state. ",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#11004, 2026-09-11. The branch predated gunbc#11003 (`0ab33d7a`, deleting the `required-v2-native` job), and its own diff touches no YAML. Every run of that head queued the deleted job, held the runner, and left the aggregate waiting; the runs were cancelled because they could not conclude. The repair was one merge of current main, after which `grep -c required-v2-native .github/workflows/witnesses.yml` at the head reads 0 and the diff is unchanged. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, and only because a human noticed the runner-hours. The detection today is a sweep somebody remembers to run. CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable -- the required floor can compare the head's job roster to the default branch's and refuse a head carrying a job the default branch has deleted, which is a decidable question about two files. NEXT TRIGGER: that check emitted into `gunbc.witness_floor_workflow`, so the refusal rides the same emission as the lanes it is about rather than living as a habit.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
